      "message": "No, if the requestedColorType is F16, we should give them F16. This should just say\n\n  return kRGBA_1010102_SkColorType;\n\nI was suggesting that we should change the code on what is now line 149:\n\n  return highPrecision ? kRGBA_F16_SkColorType : kN32_SkColorType;\n\nWe hit this case if you asked for `N32` or some format not listed here. `N32` is the exceptional case, *because* it\u0027s the default. This method gets called with `N32 to determine the default color type to use. If the client asks for `N32`, but it\u0027s a \"highPrecision\" image (which, until now, meant a PNG with 16 bits per component), we give them F16. I would expect that for a 10 bit image, we would default to 1010102, at least for an opaque image.",
